{
  "id": "ENT026",
  "title": "The Orchestra of One Note Each",
  "family": "fiction",
  "category": "cooperation",
  "premise": "Five performers want to play a recognizable original tune, but each instrument can make only one note and everyone enters at once. They turn the score into a moving marker that points to one player at a time, producing a short melody and a deliberately joyful final chord.",
  "hook": "Everybody knows one note. That is currently the problem.",
  "visible_action": "Five notes collide visually; a marker travels across five lanes; instruments activate in order; all players join at the last cue.",
  "intended_takeaway_or_theme": "Coordination can make limited contributions useful.",
  "gate": "Compose an original melody; do not imply that one particular sequence has universal emotional meaning.",
